<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to October 2 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.35 (0.35)	 one year     0.41 (0.42)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.60 (0.63)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.36 (0.36)	 three years  1.15 (1.19)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.36 (0.37)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.55 (0.58)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.31 (0.31)	 three years  1.10 (1.14)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.32 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.49 (0.52)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.27)	 three years  1.05 (1.09)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Sept 30- Oct 04:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.50 (0.56)   120-150 days  0.54 (UNQ )</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.52 (0.53)   150-180 days  0.55 (0.55)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.52 (0.53)   180-360 days  0.59 (0.56)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.53 (0.57)   over 360 days 1.28 (1.24)</p>
</text>
